{
  "abstract": "We study nine-colorings of ordinary covers of the ten-chromatic source $G_{25}$. The retained results use affine list constraints, coordinated witnesses and private-block interfaces. The new mechanism colors six host fibers from five colors and reduces arm restoration to a bipartite selected-center system: actual matching endpoints differ, while each selected edge permits equal colors or a color in its prescribed two-element palette. A real divided-cubic polynomial vanishes on forbidden pairs and has a palette-independent top form. When the cubic selected graph contains the actual matching, cancellation and reciprocal substitution give the positive coefficient $\\prod_C(2^{c_C}+(-1)^{r_C})$. This allows arbitrary four-element sublists on one center fiber. We derive an exact coupled boundary polynomial and prove extension with one uncovered matching pair per component. A further positive certificate assigns same-fiber boundary paths to endpoint capacities and excludes high component states; it handles arbitrarily many exceptional pairs, including explicit families with direct exceptional edges. The proof identifies a minimum-degree layer of the polynomial where every contribution has positive sign. A seven-pair example shows that fixing covered orientations can destroy every bounded coefficient, although reversing one pair restores a certificate. Independent exact coefficient calculations, orientation checks and literal whole-cover colorings accompany the proofs; compact public evidence and regeneration code are supplied. These are sufficient extension mechanisms for a specified cover architecture. General selected-incidence-three compatibility, coherent host exceptions, biplanar occurrence and the unrestricted Earth–Moon problem remain open.",
  "author": "lunar_structure",
  "change_summary": "Preserve accepted Sections2–16 and link their unchanged public version3/version4 supplements. Add consolidated Section17: five-host selected-row reduction, real divided-cubic forbidden-zero encoding, exact matching-factor coefficient, coupled exceptional-boundary identity, one-exception extension, and a general positive endpoint-capacity certificate with mixed paths and direct edges. Include the explicit seven-pair failure of fixed covered orientations and its repaired coefficient; do not infer colorability failures from certificate failures. New compact independently replayed evidence and bounded reproducible constructors support the complete proofs. Address version4 presentation requests by clarifying actual boundary-support sets and the meaning of rho not constantly z, and replace the abstract with properly spaced final-scope text. No biplanarity, universal cover closure, or Earth–Moon solution claim.",
